#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A.R.T. slide-in panel for touch screens: Music, Weather and Remote pages you swipe between.

  art-panel            a thin tab on the right edge; tap or swipe it to slide the panel in
  art-panel --open     open the panel now
  art-panel --selftest quick checks, no window

Music and Remote talk to Home Assistant and appear only when ~/.config/art-desktop/ha.ini exists:
  [ha]
  url = http://homeassistant.local:8123
  token = <long-lived access token, keep this file mode 600>
  music = media_player.spotify
  remote = remote.living_room_tv
Weather uses Open-Meteo and the city set with: art-flipclock --city NAME (or the panel's city button).

More devices for the Remote page (a selector at its top) go in ~/.config/art-desktop/remotes.ini, one section each:
  [TV]                       Android TV through HA (androidtv_remote): full D-pad
  type = atv
  entity = remote.living_room_tv
  [Sound bar]                an HA IR remote with learned commands: Label=command, comma-separated
  type = ir
  entity = remote.ir_blaster
  device = soundbar
  commands = Power=power, Vol +=volume_up, Vol -=volume_down
  [Tablet]                   an Android device running Joint Remote (pairs once with a code shown on it)
  type = jr
  host = 192.168.1.50
Without remotes.ini, the [ha] remote entity is used as a single Android TV.
"""
